<title>UK: Russia's Novorossiisk reopens after two-day closure.</title>
<headline>Russia's Novorossiisk reopens after two-day closure.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's leading oil export terminal at the Black Sea port of Novorossiisk reopened early on Thursday after a two-day closure because of bad weather, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>The port reopened at 0630 local time on Thursday after shutting at 0600 on Tuesday because of high winds and swell, the source said.</p>
<p>The Butron was alongside berth one and about to start loading 130,000 tonnes of Russian Urals crude. Four more crude tankers were outside the port waiting to berth.</p>
<p>Operations at other Black Sea ports at Tuapse and Odessa and at Ventspils on the Baltic were normal, the shipping source said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
